; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHAT A SKILL LOOKS LIKE GOING OFF.
;
; One block per skill, named by the skill's own Look line, and drawn from its
; layers -- every field of one is listed in data/effects/flame_arrow.duke. Two
; layer types carry nearly all of it:
;
;   RING   a ring that opens across the floor and fades late. The shape a skill
;          is RECOGNISED by. A burst of sparks says "something happened here" and
;          every skill in the game would say it the same way; a ring has a size,
;          a speed and a colour, and those three are how a player tells a nova
;          from a whirlwind at a glance without reading a word.
;   MARK   a disc that STAYS. The opposite errand: the ring says what just
;          happened, this says what is about to. The meteor's warning is the
;          whole reason it exists.
;
;          ★ A mark goes where the thing it was cast on goes. A ring belongs to
;          the SPOT it went off at and stays there, because it is an event; a mark
;          can be either, and Follows says which. A guard is a state the man is
;          in, so it travels with him and ends with him. A meteor's warning is a
;          promise about a patch of floor, so it does not move even if the mage
;          who called it walks away or dies.
;
; ★ SIZEEASE IS THE FEEL, and it is one number. At 1 a ring opens at a constant
; speed, which is what a progress bar does and what nothing in the world does;
; at 2 to 4 it leaps out and then settles, which is what a thing that was struck
; does. Everything else on these blocks is colour and size; this is the line
; between an effect and a widget.
;
; LIGHT IS THE OTHER HALF. This is a dark game and the four dynamic lights the
; terrain shader reads are the most valuable thing on the page -- a ring lit
; from a flash is a ring the room is briefly a different colour for. A LIGHT
; layer is how a skill asks for one.
;
; LAYERED, not chosen between. A cast draws its flash and its sparks first -- an
; IMPACT and a BURST -- and then opens its ring THROUGH them, so the three arrive
; as one thing. Any of them may be dropped by its own ceiling without touching
; the others.
;
; SHORT. Nothing here runs past 0.6s except the meteor's warning, which is not an
; effect so much as a promise. An effect the player has to wait out is one he
; learns to stop looking at.
;
; The knock: ShakeSeconds and ShakePower move the CAMERA'S EYE and not what it is
; looking at, so the world rattles round whatever is in the middle of the screen.
; Small numbers -- a shake that can be seen is one a player asks you to remove.
; Set both to 0 on any block to take it out, and set them to 0 everywhere to take
; the whole idea out without touching a line of code.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

; ---- the archer ----

Effect
  Name = Shot
  ; Q, the drawn shot. A tight bright ring at his feet as he lets go, and nothing
  ; else: the shot itself is the HeavyArrow, which is already the best-dressed
  ; thing in the game. This only says "that was the good one".

  Layers = [
    ; The draw, for as long as her wind-up lasts: light gathering in to the arrow as
    ; she pulls -- sparks drawn inward rather than thrown out, the one inward thing on
    ; the page -- and a glint that blooms on the last of it.
    Layer
      Name = Gather
      Type = BURST
      Texture = kit/effects/particles/star_04.png
      Blend = Additive
      Count = 24
      Radius = 12
      Life = [0.45, 0.5]
      Size = [4, 1.5]
      SizeEase = 1
      Colour = [0xFFE0A0, 0xFFFFFF]
      Alpha = [0.6, 1]
      FadeOut = 0.15
      Speed = [-24, -20]
      Direction = OUT
      Height = 7
    End

    Layer
      Name = Charge
      Type = IMPACT
      Texture = kit/effects/particles/circle_05.png
      Blend = Additive
      Cover = 0.2
      Count = 1
      Life = [0.42, 0.42]
      Size = [2, 12]
      SizeEase = -2.5
      Colour = [0xFFD080, 0xFFFFFF]
      Alpha = [0.3, 1]
      FadeOut = 0.12
      Height = 7
      TurnJitter = 0
    End

    Layer
      Name = Glint
      Type = IMPACT
      Texture = kit/effects/particles/star_07.png
      Blend = Additive
      Delay = 0.35
      Count = 1
      Life = [0.2, 0.2]
      Size = [4, 16]
      SizeEase = 3
      Colour = [0xFFFFFF, 0xFFC060]
      Alpha = [1, 0]
      FadeOut = 0.6
      Height = 7
      TurnJitter = 0
    End
  ]
End
